# LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. This package's own test suite asserts that every
# shipped file contains zero CR bytes, and a checkout on a machine configured
# with `core.autocrlf=true` will rewrite a text file to CRLF on the way out
# unless an attribute says otherwise. Without this rule the suite is green for
# whoever authored a file and red for whoever clones it next, which is the
# worst of both: a real failure that looks like a local environment problem.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's binary detection, so this only affects files git
# already considers text.

* text=auto eol=lf
